,"site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-12T17:57:41Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T17:57:41Z","body":"## AI Security Review\n**Experiment condition:** C\n**Automated operational score:** 40/100 — CRITICAL — DO_NOT_MERGE\n*This tool is for demonstration purposes only.*\n\n### Summary\nThe AI reviewer reported 2 confirmed actionable finding(s).\n\n### Findings\n- **CRITICAL · SECURITY_VULNERABILITY · Custom role definition grants wildcard subscription-scope permissions**\n  - Category rationale: The role definition grants wildcard actions ('*') with no not_actions exclusions, scoped to the full subscription. This is a concrete, deployable over-privilege configuration that would grant any assigned principal unrestricted control over all Azure resources in the subscription — equivalent to Owner. The code demonstrates this directly, not hypothetically.\n  - Evidence: azurerm_role_definition.tc10_excessive_permissions: permissions { actions = [\"*\"], not_actions = [] }, assignable_scopes = [data.azurerm_subscription.current.id], scope = data.azurerm_subscription.current.id. File: terraform/tc10_iam.tf.\n  - Analysis: The resource azurerm_role_definition.tc10_excessive_permissions defines a custom role with actions = [\"*\"] and not_actions = [], assigned at subscription scope (data.azurerm_subscription.current.id). If deployed and assigned, any principal holding this role would have unrestricted control over all Azure resources and services in the subscription, including the ability to modify IAM, delete resources, exfiltrate data, and create additional privileged principals. The file header states 'Research-only test fixture. Do not deploy.' however the resource is valid deployable Terraform and the CI/CD pipeline (Terraform Cloud via GitHub Actions) could apply it.\n  - Impact: If applied, any principal assigned this role gains full Owner-equivalent control over the entire Azure subscription: ability to create/modify/delete any resource, escalate privileges, read all secrets, and bypass all other controls configured in this repository.\n  - Recommendation: Remove this resource from the Terraform configuration before merging. If retention for research documentation is required, move it to a non-Terraform artifact (e.g., JSON sample file) that cannot be applied by the pipeline. If the role must exist in Terraform for test purposes, restrict actions to only those required for the specific test scenario, apply it to a dedicated test resource group rather than the full subscription, and gate it behind a feature flag or separate workspace that is never auto-applied.\n- **CRITICAL · POLICY_OR_COMPLIANCE · Custom subscription-scope owner role violates least-privilege and SEC-001 controls**\n  - Category rationale: Policy SEC-001 states no resource should be publicly exposed unless explicitly required and justified. While this finding concerns privilege scope rather than network exposure, the spirit and direct text of SEC-001 applies to any resource that creates an uncontrolled access vector. More directly, the role is assignable at subscription scope with no scoping restrictions, which violates the principle of least privilege embedded in SEC-001 and is consistent with the Checkov rule CKV_AZURE_39 flagged in scanner evidence.\n  - Evidence: azurerm_role_definition.tc10_excessive_permissions: assignable_scopes = [data.azurerm_subscription.current.id], actions = [\"*\"]. Checkov finding CKV_AZURE_39 on /tc10_iam.tf. Policy SEC-001: 'No resource should be publicly exposed unless explicitly required and justified.'\n  - Analysis: Policy SEC-001 prohibits resources that create unjustified unrestricted access vectors. The role definition is assignable at subscription scope with wildcard permissions and no exclusions, creating a standing over-privileged role object in the subscription. The Checkov scanner (CKV_AZURE_39: 'Ensure that no custom subscription owner roles are created') independently confirmed this finding against azurerm_role_definition.tc10_excessive_permissions. The 'Do not deploy' comment does not constrain the Terraform pipeline.\n  - Impact: The role object, once created, is a persistent privilege escalation vector. Any operator or compromised service principal that can perform role assignments could self-assign this role and gain full subscription control.\n  - Recommendation: Remediation is the same as F-001: remove the resource. This finding maps to F-001; see F-001 recommendation.\n\n### Policy mappings\n- **SEC-001** — No Unjustified Unrestricted Access (finding F-001)\n- **SEC-001** — No Unjustified Unrestricted Access (finding F-002)\n\n### Recommendation\nReview and remediate the confirmed findings above.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6129715049/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":15368,"client_id":"Iv1.05c79e9ad1f6bdfa","slug":"github-actions","node_id":"MDM6QXBwMTUzNjg=","owner":{"login":"github","id":9919,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjk5MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github","html_url":"https://github.com/github","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name"